# Shell scripts must check out with LF — bash rejects CRLF (core.autocrlf=true otherwise converts them).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Retained upstream licence manifests are EVIDENCE, not source. Their SHA-256 is recorded in
# the packaged PROVENANCE.md files and checked by crates/ferrosintesis/src/provenance.rs, so
# any line-ending conversion silently changes the bytes being attested. With core.autocrlf=true
# (the fleet default on Windows) these check out as CRLF and every recorded hash misses — on a
# fresh clone, not on the machine that committed them. `-text` disables the conversion in both
# directions. Applies at any depth, so a future pack's manifest is covered on arrival.
_readme_and_license_*.txt -text

# Same rule for an album that pins its own sources by SHA-256. `Every Voice Forward`
# ships a SHA256SUMS.txt whose hashes are taken from the committed (LF) blobs; with
# core.autocrlf=true every text entry in it fails on a fresh Windows clone while the
# binary .mid entries pass. `-text` keeps the checked-out bytes equal to the attested
# ones. build.py writes album_manifest.json with LF, so a rebuild stays verifiable too.
"albums/gpt5-6/Every Voice Forward/*.md" -text
"albums/gpt5-6/Every Voice Forward/*.py" -text
"albums/gpt5-6/Every Voice Forward/album_manifest.json" -text
"albums/gpt5-6/Every Voice Forward/SHA256SUMS.txt" -text
